 Workarounds
 ===========
 
+KK_WORKAROUND_16
+----------------
+| macOS version: 26.x
+| Metal ticket: Not reported
+| Metal ticket status:
+| CTS test failure: ``dEQP-GL45-ES31.functional.shaders.opaque_type_indexing.sampler.dynamically_uniform.tessellation_evaluation.*``, ``dEQP-GL45-ES31.functional.tessellation_geometry_interaction.render.passthrough.tessellate_*_passthrough_geometry_no_change``
+| Comments:
+
+A compute pipeline built with a small ``maxTotalThreadsPerThreadgroup``
+miscompiles a large kernel: a value that every thread computes identically
+comes back correct for the first eight threads of each SIMD group and as zero
+for the rest, so a sampled texel or a loaded patch vertex silently becomes
+zero. Whether a given kernel is affected depends on how many values are live
+at once, which is why removing one texture lookup, storing each result as soon
+as it is produced, or any unrelated change to the emitted code moves the
+failure to a different shader instead of removing it. Raising the limit, or
+leaving it unset, compiles the same MSL correctly.
+
+The stages a graphics pipeline emulates in compute - vertex, tessellation
+control and evaluation, geometry, transform feedback and line rasterization -
+inline the whole application shader and are launched with a threadgroup size
+the driver picks, not one the application asked for. Compile them without a
+thread limit. Application compute shaders keep the size they declare, which is
+the size Metal has to honour. Disabling this workaround restores the launch
+threadgroup size as the compiled limit.
+
+| Log:
+| 2026-09-07: Workaround implemented
+
 KK_WORKAROUND_15
 ----------------
 | macOS version: 26.x
