+
+/* Attaching a geometry shader that re-emits the tessellated primitive
+ * unchanged must not change the rasterized image.  The tessellation
+ * evaluation stage is emulated in compute when a geometry shader is present
+ * and consumed by the hardware vertex stage when it is not, so both consumers
+ * must place, order and shade the same primitives.  Additive blending makes a
+ * duplicated, dropped or reordered primitive visible as a brightness change.
+ */
+
+#define VK_NO_PROTOTYPES
